   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">Hi,</font><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">First time poster here!</font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">Here&#39;s the model I&#39;m trying to create:</font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\"><br></font></div><div>\r\n\t\t\r\n\t\r\n\t\r\n\t\t<div title=\"Page 1\">\r\n\t\t\t<div>\r\n\t\t\t\t<div>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t<p><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">z<span style=\"vertical-align:-1pt\">t </span>∼NB(μ<span style=\"vertical-align:-1pt\">t</span>, k),   μ<span style=\"vertical-align:-1pt\">t </span>=Xb + φμ<span style=\"vertical-align:-1pt\">t</span><span style=\"vertical-align:-1pt\">−</span><span style=\"vertical-align:-1pt\">1 </span>+αz<span style=\"vertical-align:-1pt\">t</span><span style=\"vertical-align:-1pt\">−</span><span style=\"vertical-align:-1pt\">1 </span>+(1−φ−α)μ </font></p>\r\n\t\t\t\t</div>\r\n\t\t\t</div>\r\n\t\t</div></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">where X is my design matrix, b is fixed effect, k is shape, α, φ, μ are positive, and  α + φ &lt; 1. I got the idea from this publication:</font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">Forecasting the intermittent demand for slow-moving inventories: A modelling approach, Snyder et al, International Journal of Forecasting<br></font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">Here&#39;s the stan code I&#39;ve written:</font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\"><br></font></div><div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">data { </font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">  int&lt;lower=1&gt; N;</font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">  int Y[N];</font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">  int&lt;lower=1&gt; K;</font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">  vector[N] X;</font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">} </font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">transformed data { </font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">} </font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">parameters { </font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">  real b;</font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">  real&lt;lower=0&gt; shape;</font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">  real&lt;lower=0&gt; mu;    </font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">  real&lt;lower=0&gt; alpha;</font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">  real&lt;lower=0&gt; tmp;</font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">} </font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">transformed parameters { </font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">  vector[N] eta;</font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">  real&lt;lower=0&gt; phi;</font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">  phi &lt;- 1 - alpha - tmp;</font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">  eta[1] &lt;- log(Y[1]);</font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">  for (t in 2:N) {</font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">    eta[t] &lt;- X[t] * b + (1 - phi - alpha) * mu + phi * eta[t - 1] + alpha * Y[t - 1];</font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">  }</font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">} </font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">model { </font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">  shape ~ gamma(0.01, 0.01); </font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">  alpha ~ normal(0.5, 0.5);</font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">  tmp ~ normal(0.5, 0.5);</font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\"> </font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">  Y ~ neg_binomial_2_log(eta, shape); </font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">}</font></div></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">and here is my stan call:</font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\"><br></font></div><div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">fit = stan(model_name =&quot;negbinomial&quot;, </font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">           model_code = stan_code, </font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">           data = data , </font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">           iter = 2000, </font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">           chains = 4, </font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">           control = list(adapt_delta = 0.95),</font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">           verbose = FALSE)</font></div></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">However, the fit doesn&#39;t go very well. I get these warnings:</font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">validate transformed params: phi is -9.65355e-05, but must be greater than or equal to 0      1<br></font></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\"><br></font></div><div><pre style=\"box-sizing:border-box;overflow:auto;line-height:17.0001px;word-break:break-all;word-wrap:break-word;color:rgb(0,0,0);border-radius:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;vertical-align:baseline;background-color:transparent\"><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">Warning message:\r\n: There were 3304 divergent transitions after warmup. Increasing adapt_delta above 0.95 may help.</font></pre><pre style=\"box-sizing:border-box;overflow:auto;line-height:17.0001px;word-break:break-all;word-wrap:break-word;color:rgb(0,0,0);border-radius:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;vertical-align:baseline;background-color:transparent\"><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\">Warning message:\r\n: Examine the pairs() plot to diagnose sampling problems</font></pre></div><div><font face=\"times new roman, serif\" size=\"2\"><br></font></div><div>What can I do to improve the fit?</div></div>"
    ]
