te><div><br>One instance of that is nothing to worry about.<br> </div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div></div><div>And how can I exclude Y[1]? Rhat value for mu[1] is NaN. This shouldn&#39;t cause problems, right?</div></div></div></blockquote><div><br><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><div>The problem is that you are doing mu[1] &lt;- Y[1] and then modeling Y[1] with mu[1].  You could either put a marginal prior on mu[1] or omit Y[1] from the likelihood.<br><br>Ben<br><br></div></div></div></div></div></div></blockquote></div>"
